@echo off
rem Copy this file to  paths.cmd  (same folder as CoD4toSOF2.exe) and edit it.
rem compile_cod4_map.bat reads it on every Compile, from the GUI as well as
rem when you run the .bat by hand.
rem
rem Every setting below uses "if not defined", so anything the GUI already
rem passes wins and this file only fills in what is missing. Do not change
rem that to a plain "set" for the path variables, or compiling from the GUI
rem will use these paths instead of the ones in the GUI.

rem ---------------------------------------------------------------- paths
rem Only needed when you run compile_cod4_map.bat directly; the GUI's Compile
rem button passes all three itself.

rem q3map2.exe from NetRadiant or GtkRadiant
if not defined Q3MAP2   set "Q3MAP2=C:\Games\NetRadiant\q3map2.exe"

rem The folder that CONTAINS base\ -- not base\ itself
if not defined GAMEROOT set "GAMEROOT=C:\Games\Soldier of Fortune II - Double Helix"

rem CoD4toSOF2's output folder: the one holding <mapname>\maps, \shaders, ...
if not defined OUTDIR   set "OUTDIR=C:\CoD4toSOF2\output"

rem ------------------------------------------------------------- lighting
rem These are not set by the GUI, so they belong here if you want to change
rem them. Uncomment and edit. Every one of them needs a Compile to take
rem effect, because the lighting is baked into the .bsp.
rem
rem q3map2 turns a light value into a byte as
rem     v = pow(v/255, 1/GAMMA) * 255
rem     if EXPOSURE: v = v * (1 - exp(-v/EXPOSURE)) * 255 / v
rem
rem GAMMA defaults to 1.6. The CS:S pipeline's 2.2 lifted the midtones hard -
rem 128 came out at 186, and everything from 192 up landed within a few values
rem of 255, so grey metal and snow read as flat white. NOTE: cod4mat2shader
rem derives the sun intensity from LIGHT_GAMMA, which must match this. Change
rem both or neither.
rem set "COD4TOSOF2_GAMMA=1.6"
rem
rem EXPOSURE (0 = off) adds an exponential roll-off AFTER gamma, so nothing
rem reaches pure white and highlights keep their detail. It flattens the
rem image a little: at 200 the brightest value becomes 184 instead of 255.
rem Try it if lowering gamma alone still clips.
rem set "COD4TOSOF2_EXPOSURE=200"
rem
rem GRIDSCALE boosts the light grid, which lights the model_static props and
rem anything vertex-lit - not the lightmaps. Raise it if the props look dark
rem against the world, lower it if they glow.
rem set "COD4TOSOF2_GRIDSCALE=4.59"
rem
rem BOUNCE is q3map2 radiosity, and it is OFF (0) because it does not finish
rem on a big map. Measured on mp_strike: the direct light pass runs on 76
rem lights and takes 34 seconds, and -bounce 1 turns those into 122,201
rem diffuse lights over 2.45 million luxels - still running after two hours.
rem CoD's own radiosity numbers (sunradiosity / radiosityscale in the
rem worldspawn) go into q3map_skyLight instead, which costs nothing. Setting
rem this to 1 is worth a try on a small map - mp_shipment has 162 clusters
rem where Strike has 1030 - but expect hours on anything Strike's size.
rem set "COD4TOSOF2_BOUNCE=0"
